urement and final-control equipment to meet required range, capacity, response, and process conditions. Within Final Control Elements, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of sizing principles within Process Control and Instrumentation, particularly where the Final Control Elements module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of sizing principles, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'sizing principles; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of sizing principles, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Process Control and Instrumentation', 'Active'), ('KCR_000754', 'first-order and higher-order models', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Process Control and Instrumentation', 'Technical Concept', 'Dynamic process models representing one or more energy-storage or response modes.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of first-order and higher-order models within Process Control and Instrumentation, particularly where the Process Dynamics module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of first-order and higher-order models, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Dynamic process models representing one or more energy-storage or response modes. Within Process Dynamics, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of first-order and higher-order models within Process Control and Instrumentation, particularly where the Process Dynamics module establishes its technical context. Key technical considera